        "node_id": "n_2_c49d2e",
        "thought_text": "Greedy Algorithm is not suitable here because it does not always lead to the optimal solution. Instead, we should consider a different approach that ensures we use the fewest number of packages to reach exactly \\( n \\) shovels. One effective strategy is to start with the largest possible package size and work our way down until we reach exactly \\( n \\) shovels. This ensures that we minimize the number of packages used.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
