        "node_id": "n_7_979cad",
        "thought_text": "Iterative Reduction Strategy with Correct Handling:\n\nTo ensure the correct minimum number of packages, we should iterate from the largest possible package size down to 1. For each package size, we calculate how many times we can use it without exceeding the required number of shovels. We then subtract the total shovels obtained from using that package size and move to the next smaller package size. This approach guarantees that we use the fewest number of packages to reach exactly \\( n \\) shovels.",
